WEBVTT

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:51.790
Reload.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:57.390
Note: German for "Fire!"

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.630
Feuer!
Note: German for "Fire!"

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.580
What's the matter?

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.780
The game's still on.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:09.970
Reload.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.980
You've gotta run if you want the money!

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.110
Come on, come on!

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.560
Your "marksmanship" has improved.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.080
Hunting is the pastime of the nobility, is it not?

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.280
I say, Hosslow.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.190
Don't you think this is a wonderful era?

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.840
Noblemen and commoners,

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.350
the haves and the have-nots.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.590
The gap between the rich and the poor is this evident.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:46.360
This is a truly wonderful era!

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.110
Sorry...

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.630
I'm sorry, Mer-kun.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.700
I couldn't protect you.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.630
You liked sausages, right?

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.610
Mer-kun, you can't go around biting people.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.400
So, you got demoted.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.430
That's so cruel.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:42.550
You're no longer a Corporal, but just a Courier First Class.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.210
Eat this and cheer up, okay?

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.030
He's pretty late...

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:12.430
Isn't he just lost?

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.060
He did look kind of dumb.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:16.810
He's late!

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.490
How dare he be late the first day after being transferred here!

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:21.740
Now there, LT!

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.240
You can't pull your sword out inside the facility!

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.310
Let go of me!

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.880
I-I think he might just be lost or something.
What shall we do, Captain Hunks?

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:28.400
Leave them be.
I-I think he might just be lost or something.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:28.850
Leave them be.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:28.880
What's so funny?!

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.850
But don't you think it'd be better if I did something?
What's so funny?!

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:32.680
But don't you think it'd be better if I did something?

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:32.780
Wait, wait.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.030
You don't have to do anything.
Wait, wait.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:34.770
You don't have to do anything.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:35.880
Calm down!

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:37.560
N-No!

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:44.130
Well, I've just been told that I could get new clothing if I came here.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:45.750
No, no!

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.660
This is an army facility.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:50.280
We can't let anyone in without proper permission.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.140
Permission? Oh, here...

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.790
Randel Oland...

00:04:58.730 --> 00:04:59.690
Corporal?

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:04.980
"You are hereby assigned to Imperial Army S.S.III effective today."

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.530
Captain Hunks, I made some tea for you.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:15.710
Thanks.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:19.170
Umm, I just realized that...

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.560
...when the new Corporal comes in today,

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.320
I'm going to become his superior, right?

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.760
Don't you have Mercury as your subordinate already?

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.720
The fact that Mer-kun and I are friends comes before the fact that he's my underling.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.520
Okay, I see that,

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.840
but where did your friend go now?

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:48.240
Mer-kun was right here just now...

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.220
Oh, no!

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:53.840
If he goes to bite another person, then he's really going to be thrown out this time!

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:55.280
Mer-kun!

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:55.390
Hey!

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:56.370
Where are you?!
Hey!

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:56.820
Where are you?!

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:00.330
Eh?

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:02.870
Section III is one building the other way?

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:08.150
Run!

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.560
Get out of the way!

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.840
Let us recite now...

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:17.130
...regarding the proper manner in which we need to portray ourselves!

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.770
All men, repeat after me!

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.640
"We are..."

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:23.260
We... whoa!!

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.110
Not "whoa"... "are"!

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.650
Don't stretch out the sound in weird places!

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:30.100
Generally speaking, you guys have been-

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:36.660
Good day.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.070
Whoa!

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.370
I have brought Corporal Oland.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.710
Well, our LT is a very straight and stubborn person,

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.920
so don't get too excited.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:51.210
You won't get promoted even if you work hard.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.210
Section III is like the gathering place for people with nowhere to go.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:57.610
Most of our tasks are either filing documents or inspection trips.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:00.150
Our lives are pretty safe, but we won't get any chances for glory either.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:03.790
They call us "the peaceful and easy-going Imperial S.S. III".

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.240
Peaceful... and... easy-going...

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:12.540
Well, sometimes we get some Swiss cheese action like last time.

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:15.120
I... actually like that...

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.600
...that it's peaceful and such...

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:26.960
Hey, hey, let the LT be the only hot-blooded person, please.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.970
Let's take it easy.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.560
But you sure are tall.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.370
You're my subordinate starting today,

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.660
you got that, big guy? Subordinate!

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:38.270
That sounds pretty good.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:39.980
All men aboard!

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:45.910
He seems like a nice person.

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:48.680
It's almost as if he's not a soldier.

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:50.610
Yeah.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.340
You don't "smell" like a soldier,

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:01.780
but, your combat capabilities are very abnormal, quite frankly.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.250
So basically, that Wol...

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.460
...Wolkinson?

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:10.710
Viscount Wolkins' territory.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.940
Our mission this time is to give administrative education to the feudal lord there, right?

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.660
What, is he evading taxes?

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:23.020
No, Section III received a petition saying the public peace there has been disturbed.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.430
Hmm, and who sent it?

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:28.980
Well, we don't know the name of the sender.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:35.330
Heck, so we just need to do some preaching to this feudal lord that's gone too far, right?

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:37.360
Piece of cake, man!

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.160
Oreld, don't be so relaxed already!

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:48.200
I'm feeling chills on the back of my neck.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:51.300
"Something" is always going to happen when I feel this.

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.680
What a lifeless town.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:02.320
It's like this pretty much everywhere.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:04.770
No one has food or jobs or anything.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.690
There's just plenty of rubble and free time.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.340
That doesn't seem like the only thing...

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:13.640
A funeral procession?

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:15.390
That's weird.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:16.940
You think so?

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.280
Dead bodies aren't that rare.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.190
Besides, how many people do you think died from that war-

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:21.660
Fool!
Besides, how many people do you think died from that war-

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.120
Fool!

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:23.770
It's a post-war time right now.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.770
Our country's security has not fallen to a degree...

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.420
...that it's normal for three people to die at the same time.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.650
I wonder what happened then.

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:34.100
It's a game.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.390
They lost the game.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.430
That bastard of a feudal lord...

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:42.240
Stop, old man.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.800
He's nobility.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.560
We can't go against him.

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:52.710
What the hell is this?

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.490
It's cooked rare!

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.310
M-Master...

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:58.980
B-But that's what you instructed me to do yesterday...

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:02.190
...that you wanted your steak rare and bloody...

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.560
F-Forgive me.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:07.510
I'll prepare a new one right away!

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.880
Oh yeah, come to think...

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.480
I haven't fed the pets lately!

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:23.950
It's okay.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.680
Go ahead and eat.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.420
Get the Viscount out here now!

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:33.170
Where is he?!

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:34.510
W-Wait!

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.660
The master is dining right now!

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:38.860
Here?

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:39.650
He's in here, right?

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.740
Get up, you bastard!

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:46.450
We are the Imperial Army S.S. III
Pumpkin Scissors platoon!

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:49.110
Section III?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.250
Pump?

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.060
I've heard your doings from the citizens!

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:54.660
Scoundrels like you...

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.630
Ah, those people...

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:57.690
Your very own citizens...

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:00.820
...that you were supposed to protect...

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:04.140
Please calm down, LT.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.000
We ask of you, Viscount!

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:10.630
You make your citizens "targets" and chase them around in a tank...

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:13.330
We heard you indulge yourself in that kind of delinquency.

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.380
Is this the truth?

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.010
Delinquency?

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:23.040
Don't be saying such impolite things.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.400
That's... what shall I call it...

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.240
...it's like a game!

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.730
How dare you!

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:31.410
You're saying this is a game where you fire at people who can't resist?!

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:32.580
That's right!

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.040
They use their own lives as chips.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.340
If they manage to survive the tank, they make a fortune.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.560
For these commoners that I have chosen as 'targets',

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:45.760
I have prepared enough gold for them to live out the rest of their entire lives.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.230
Of course,

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:50.720
no target has been able to survive this game.

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:52.690
Just because...

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:55.530
Just because you were born a noble,

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.650
you use people as if they were chess pieces?

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:02.950
Don't get too conceited, you small dictator in your own little world!

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:10.200
That's a great expression you have there.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.460
What?!

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:15.300
Hosslow here was a former tank soldier in the army.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:18.200
He knows of several interesting stories.

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:21.470
I have heard this story from other tank soldiers,

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:28.280
that there is a propaganda unit set up so that the military can use the national budget more easily.

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:35.130
A cheery unit which, by undertaking this excuse for an act of "war relief" in front of commoners,

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:39.690
appeases the dissatisfaction and complaints they have towards their country...

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:44.950
That's the true purpose of the
Imperial Army S.S. III Pumpkin Scissors.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:52.050
What's the name of your act today? Administrative education?

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:54.930
It sure is pretty hard to grab the hearts of the citizens, eh?!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:01.960
You filthy snob who's feeding off the post-war situation...

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:03.920
Viscount Wolkins!

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:07.220
We regard you as a war aggravator...

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.100
...and will proceed to remove you from this territory!

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:14.600
I played along with your act thinking it was one...

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.060
Enough...

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:21.440
Become my targets.

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:30.720
Why does the peaceful and easy-going Section III end up in trouble like this?

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:31.950
You're right.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:35.910
It's a great view, isn't it, Ms. Second Lieutenant!

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:39.490
That's a first-class seat for you to see the entire field of the game.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.520
Hey, you monkeys!

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.260
I'll give you only five minutes.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.260
Run as far as you want!

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.600
Well, let's not waste his kindness...

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.680
Hey, Oreld!

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:59.450
If all three of us stick together, we're going to be an easy bull's eye.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:02.970
Why don't we do what we can with these?

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:04.260
You idiot.

00:14:04.260 --> 00:14:06.970
As if crappy bullets like that would work against a tank.

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:12.640
That rich kid knows this, and that's why he didn't disarm us.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:13.760
Right.

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.810
Soldiers, eh?

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:20.250
Finally, some prey worth hunting down.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:22.140
In situations like this,

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:25.130
the best thing to do is to run away.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.280
Ta-da.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:29.580
They don't call you "stockade escape artist" for nothing, huh?

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:31.060
All right, big guy.

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:32.080
Let's start with you.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:34.680
No, you first, Sergeant Major.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.450
I don't plan on dying,

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:38.800
but I don't plan on letting others die either.

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:42.220
You are my first subordinate, after all.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:44.400
I see.

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:46.190
It was you people...

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.530
...who sent out the petition.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.110
But I don't understand.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.950
Why do you not point your guns at the Viscount?

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.270
He... he's a noble!

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:59.430
We commoners can't point the gun at him.

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:01.250
You can't because he's a noble?

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:02.820
You won't pull the trigger?

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.770
I've heard of this story among tank soldiers.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:13.480
If you see foot soldiers carrying a blue steel lantern, don't think they are your allies.

00:15:13.670 --> 00:15:15.720
But you must not turn them into enemies, either.

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:19.740
That lantern is a reactor that will light up the bearer's soul-

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:20.980
That's enough.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.350
What kind of fairy tale is that?

00:15:23.350 --> 00:15:24.060
Preposterous!

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:28.040
No one can challenge nobles... challenge me!

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.070
This is that sort of era.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:32.990
Corporal.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.480
About what the Viscount said earlier,

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.710
Section III is still the army,

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:42.120
but we don't choose how we are born,

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.240
whether it's organizations or people.

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:49.230
Is that lantern from your former unit?

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.870
Ah, what was its name?

00:15:52.750 --> 00:15:55.760
901-ATT...

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:59.380
My name is Alice L. Malvin,

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.780
the third daughter of the Malvin family,

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.190
one of the Thirteen Appointed Families.

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:08.030
You're a princess from the nobility?

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:09.070
See?

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.310
A commoner can point a gun at a noble.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.220
Now then,

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:18.670
which target should I start aiming at?

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.690
What's all this about?

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.150
It doesn't matter if it's just a bullet,

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:27.130
fire for your own honor!

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:29.260
LT!

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:31.320
Damn then...

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:32.830
I'll punish them when I get back!

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:37.010
Okay.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:38.680
Now! Disperse!

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:40.310
Corporal!

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:41.700
That idiot!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.590
Nobles...

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:44.860
Commoners...

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:46.850
Imperial Army S.S. III...

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.490
901... Anti-Tank Trooper...

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.950
That was the unit I came from.

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:00.130
That's right...

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.370
It's not how we are born that matters.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:04.880
What matters...

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:07.580
...is how we live!

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:13.660
Did you see that?

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:15.200
I got him with one shot!

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:19.970
"They will come forth along with the blue will o' the wisps..."

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.260
That fairy tale again?

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:26.900
How did it go?

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:27.720
Reload.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:30.900
Hurry and reload!

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.040
He's coming!

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:34.490
Feuer!

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:37.400
I got him this time!

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.290
Reload!

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:43.370
Hurry and reload!

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:47.730
What the hell is he?

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.170
A creature from legend?

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:55.170
Hey Hosslow... what is he?

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.370
Even if their eyes are scorched...

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:05.270
Even if their arms are writhing...

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:07.850
They will never stop marching ahead...

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:10.370
Guided by the will o' the wisp...

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:13.090
They will force their way and shoot at point-blank distance.

00:18:13.390 --> 00:18:15.200
The footsteps that have thrown away life...

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.130
The trigger that brings death...

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.730
They're the fairy tale on the battle field...

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:23.650
The 901-Anti Tank Trooper...

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:26.970
The soldiers that disregard their own lives...

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:30.890
Gespenst Jäger!

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:43.790
Reload...

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:46.810
Right, I need to reload...

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:48.340
No, it's useless.

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:50.210
I can't hit him no matter how many rounds I fire.

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.620
Because...

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:52.680
Because up until now...

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:54.810
I've only been able to shoot people that were running away.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:56.350
Okay, I get it!

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:59.610
You win the game.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:01.780
Hey, hey... hey!

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.080
You win! You win the game!

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:05.100
It's over!

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:05.700
Okay?

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:07.090
Don't shoot me, yo...

00:19:07.090 --> 00:19:09.620
I'm a human... not a target...

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:13.750
Corporal!

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:14.860
Are you okay?

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:15.930
Don't worry!

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:17.410
I'm going to save you now!

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:28.810
I won't let you die!

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:46.830
You used your back to protect me?

00:19:47.260 --> 00:19:48.040
No...

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.280
Sorry...

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.500
You guys think you've won?!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:00.600
What's gonna happen after beating me?

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:02.610
Will less people die from hunger?

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.640
Will epidemics disappear?

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:05.460
Huh?!

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:07.240
You guys are just-

00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:10.130
We all know...

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:12.340
Shut up, you idiot!

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.030
Ruptured left eardrum...

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:25.560
Part of the left trapezius ripped...

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:28.310
Three of your lower ribs are broken...

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:29.770
Abrasions on your back...

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:31.450
...among other injuries...

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:35.250
I can't believe you can end up with so many injuries...

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:38.110
I don't mind bearing injuries from combat.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.290
But if the world isn't going to change...

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:42.720
The world?!

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:45.460
You can actually see that far when you're that tall?

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:47.760
You're no different than the Viscount then.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:54.160
This was written to everyone in Section III.

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:59.600
"We give you our humblest gratitude for the other day."

00:21:00.100 --> 00:21:03.060
"After that, we asked for vacation,"

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:06.200
"and decided that we'd try our best back in our hometown."

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:09.870
"Of course, as to how we're going to live,"

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:11.820
"or how we can become happy,"

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.490
"no one knows yet."

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:18.210
"But, the honor that the LT reminded us of..."

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:20.700
"...and that something you all protected for us..."

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:23.530
"We will believe in that and proudly..."

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:26.360
"...take steps forward--as much as we can."

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.430
Don't look too far ahead.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:32.410
Just look at what's in front.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:34.390
It'll be there...

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.010
...the meaning to our battle.

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:39.340
Yes, sir.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:44.080
The long war has corrupted society...

00:21:44.560 --> 00:21:46.490
...and has spread many evils throughout.

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:51.880
However, there is a unit that exists to fight against these war damages.

00:21:52.930 --> 00:21:57.820
The unit's name is Imperial Army S.S. III Pumpkin Scissors!

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:33.910
Mer-kun, the lieutenant seems a bit odd.

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:35.500
It's like she doesn't have any energy in her.

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:37.970
I wonder if she ate breakfast before coming here.

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:41.700
Next time, "For That is a Precious Thing".

00:23:41.700 --> 00:23:43.860
Come get us if you're not scared!
